      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hi Noriro! This is a feature of Valve's driver for the Index controllers. It enhances finger expression with other information from the controller such as rotation and position relative to your headset tracking. After the Input2.0 update we now use the skeletal hand data that the Index controllers provide directly, so you can see more finger motion because of this. However, we got feedback that some users prefer the old way, (or some avatars work better with the old way), so there's an option in the Action Menu's \"Quick Actions\" section, the same place you adjust avatar scale. The option is called \"Legacy Fingers\" and the toggle is saved per-avatar. You can read more about this in our Input2.0 FAQ under the section \"My avatar's fingers look/move weird now, how do I go back to how it was before?\" at this link: https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/input-20-faq",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
